title: Ischaemic Gut Injury
---

# Ischaemic Gut Injury

- **Definition** - insufficient perfusion to the gut resulting in cellular hypoxia
- **Etiology of ischaemic gut injury:**
  - <u>Local hypoperfusion</u> (arterial occlusion) - embolic complication, local thrombosis, vasculitis
  - <u>Generalised hypoperfusion</u> - severe hypotension, venous insufficiency
- **Principles of presentation:**
  - <u>Dependent on onset</u> - acute vs chronic
  - <u>Dependent of vessel involved</u> - SB vs colonic
